      "summary": "Paris police have issued a five‑day ban on protests within 100 metres of ten secondary schools and five universities from 16 to 20 November. The order aims to curb weeks of blockades, property damage and clashes that have accompanied protests that began in September over school conditions and broader cost‑of‑living grievances.",
      "why": "The measure is intended to protect students, staff and public order by limiting further disruption and violence at educational sites.",
